[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known. Read by tenant, form and
body, its reports describe three problems. Each has its own ticket and its own fix.

<Callout kind="warn">
The one queued parser fix closes only the first row. The other two stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="patrykkopycinski/mega-what-it-shows" tickets={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day-move': 3 }} />

## How each report is placed

1. **One id, one report.** The export repeats some ids. Each counts once.
2. **One-day move.** The desk read these reports as a one-day shift (`desk-notes.json`): Tuesday
   became Monday, every June booking one day off, Lisbon and Toronto seeing different days, an
   invite that arrived before the booking. A month/day flip never moves a date by one day, so the
   parser fix cannot close them.
3. **hint.** The report came through booking-v3's form. That form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the
   date field and reads the answer the tenant's way, day first. People type what the hint says.
4. **parser.** Everything else from a day-first tenant: the shared parser reads the date month first.

The tenant decides the cause, not the reporter's browser. Intake's tag comes from the browser
locale, so it disagrees with the tenant on dozens of reports; the "intake tagged as" column shows
how far. All numbers on this page are computed from the export at render time.

## What changes on the desk

- #4471 is not "one issue, one fix". Track the three tickets above.
- A subject match ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) says nothing about cause.
  Merge on tenant, form and what the body describes.

